<article class="env-lemma" id="0DVB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DVB">Lemma <span data-tag="0DVB">10.78.9</span>.</a> Let $R$ be ring. Let $L$, $M$, $N$ be $R$-modules. The canonical map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ R(M, N) \otimes _ R L \to \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ R(M, N \otimes _ R L)  \]
</div>
  <p> is an isomorphism if $M$ is finite projective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/00NX" data-tag="00NX">10.78.2</a> we see that $M$ is finitely presented as well as finite locally free. By Lemmas <a href="/tag/0583" data-tag="0583">10.10.2</a> and <a href="/tag/00DL" data-tag="00DL">10.12.16</a> formation of the left and right hand side of the arrow commutes with localization. We may check that our map is an isomorphism after localization, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00EO" data-tag="00EO">10.23.2</a>. Thus we may assume $M$ is finite free. In this case the lemma is immediate. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>